{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_11-29-07-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsrc=open('check-harness-snapshot.go').read()\n# new harness: same scenario, but the receiver's TrailingLogs is zero so installSnapshot really compacts the log\nsrc=src.replace('TestAssuranceSnapshotInstalledCommitContext','TestAssuranceSnapshotCompactedCommitContext')\nsrc=src.replace('snapshot-installed-commit-context','snapshot-compacted-commit-context')\nsrc=src.replace('assuranceSnapEvent','assuranceSnapCmpEvent')\nsrc=src.replace('assuranceSnapFSM','assuranceSnapCmpFSM')\nsrc=src.replace('assuranceSnapSnapshot','assuranceSnapCmpSnapshot')\n# receiver config: TrailingLogs 0 so compaction removes the bootstrap entry\nimport re\nhead, tail = src.split('rcvConf.TrailingLogs = 100000',1)\nsrc = head + 'rcvConf.TrailingLogs = 0' + tail\nopen('check-harness-snapshot-compacted.go','w').write(src)\n# plan: copy the first snapshot plan, adjust ids and the description of the variation\nplan=json.load(open('check-plan-snapshot.json'))\nplan['description']=(\\\"Second scenario of the same requirement, removing the first artifact's limitation that the log was left intact: the receiving node is \\\"\n \\\"configured with no trailing logs, so installing the snapshot really compacts the log it was holding, and the harness then records the same commit context. \\\"\n \\\"Discriminator: the commit index the installing node publishes once its log has been truncated at the snapshot index. Observation: the receiver's commit index \\\"\n \\\"compared with the index the snapshot established, with its applied index, last index and state recorded beside it. Control: the same source-produced snapshot \\\"\n \\\"and the same install path as the first scenario, with the receiver's trailing-log setting reported in the event.\\\")\nplan['harness']['description']=\\\"TestAssuranceSnapshotCompactedCommitContext: the commit index published by a node that installed a committed snapshot after its log was compacted\\\"\nplan['harness']['semantic_changes']=[\n \\\"No target file is modified; the harness adds one external test file to the captured package.\\\",\n \\\"The receiving node is configured with no trailing logs, so it holds at least one log entry before the install and the install's compaction really truncates the log, unlike the first scenario which left it intact.\\\",\n \\\"The snapshot is produced by a real single-voter leader through the public Snapshot API and delivered through the module's own InmemTransport install path, as in the first scenario.\\\",\n \\\"Only the InstallSnapshot RPC is routed to the receiver and its election timeouts are long, so nothing else changes it inside the prefix.\\\"]\nplan['harness']['legality']['applicability']=(\\\"A voter node that installs a source-produced snapshot while configured with no trailing logs, so its log is truncated at the snapshot index, \\\"\n \\\"observed before any later AppendEntries. The harness reports the receiver's state, applied index and last index beside the compared value.\\\")\nplan['observable_properties'][0]['trigger']={'field':'op','op':'eq','value':'snapshot-compacted-commit-context'}\nplan['observable_properties'][0]['description']=(\\\"After the node admitted by 'admit' installed a snapshot at the index that node had committed and applied, and its log was \\\"\n \\\"truncated there, the installing node's published commit index must be that index. Within this prefix the receiver's own last index is the admitted index, so a commit \\\"\n \\\"index below it is below the committed state it has just applied and equality is exactly the requirement.\\\")\nplan['monitors'][0]['id']='m-snapshot-compacted-commit-context'\nplan['monitors'][0]['checker_id']='p-snapshot-compacted-commit-context'\nplan['observable_properties'][0]['checker_id']='p-snapshot-compacted-commit-context'\nplan['uncertainties']=[\n \\\"The observation is a single prefix immediately after the install and does not measure how long the value stays low in a live cluster.\\\",\n \\\"The receiver's log is truncated, so the prefix cannot tell whether the value would differ if entries remained; the first scenario covers the intact-log case.\\\",\n \\\"The equality encoding coincides with not-below only because the receiver's own last index is the admitted index inside this prefix.\\\"]\nplan['harness']['description']=plan['harness']['description']\nplan['claim_id']='c-snapshot-install-commit-context'\nplan['binding_ids']=['bind-raft-install-snapshot-commit']\njson.dump(plan, open('check-plan-snapshot-compacted.json','w'), indent=1)\nprint('wrote harness and plan')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
